# 🐧 REMnux Malware Analysis & Forensics Workstation (Kasm-Enhanced)

An advanced malware analysis and reverse-engineering environment built on top of `squirrelworksllc/ubuntu-noble-core`. This image seamlessly pairs the full REMnux SaltStack software catalog with the lightweight, high-performance runtime performance of modern Kasm Workspaces.

## ✔️ Included Tool Ecosystem

*   **Reverse Engineering & Disassembly:** Ghidra, Radare2, Cutter, ltrace, strace
*   **Behavioral Analysis:** Wireshark, INetSim, fakenet-ng scripts, network logging hooks
*   **Code & Script Analysis:** Visual Studio Code (pre-configured), Python3 toolkit, Oletools, YARA, Volatility 3
*   **Document & PE Forensics:** PDFiD, PDF-Parser, Pecheck, PyMMC, Wine binary compatibility layer
*   **Web Browsing:** Enterprise-stable Mozilla Firefox and Google Chrome sandboxed profiles

## 🎯 Purpose

This workstation provides a standardized, immutable, and completely isolated sandbox environment designed specifically for malware analysts, security incident responders, and forensic researchers. It is tailored for:

*   Executing interactive behavioral analysis on untrusted samples safely inside container boundaries.
*   Conducting static code dissection and automated unpacking workflows.
*   Serving as a reproducible remote forensics workstation within the Kasm 1.18 platform architecture.
